  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The proposed development for x2 self-contained flats will result in the loss of a 3-bedroom family dwellinghouse which is the type of housing in high demand within the Borough and which policies seek to protect.&amp;nbsp; The quality of the accommodation provided at the site will be reduced. The negative impact&amp;nbsp;of the proposal regarding the loss of this type of housing outweighs any significant benefit. As such, having regard to the presumption in favour of sustainable development, on balance the principle of development is considered unacceptable and contrary to:- National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, February 2019); -Policies GG4, H1, H2 and H9 of the London Plan (March 2021); -Policies CM1, CM2 and CC1 of the Core Strategy DPD (July 2010); -Policy BC4 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011); -Policies SPDG1, SP3 and DMH4&amp;nbsp; of the Draft Local Plan&amp;nbsp;(Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021); -Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (GLA, March 2016, Updated August 2017); -London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Housing Delivery Test Action Plan 2020.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails&amp;nbsp;to provide an acceptable cooking, eating and living (CEL) area floorspace for the first floor flat,&amp;nbsp;and as such the dwellings do not provide suitable and sustainable living environments for future occupiers.&amp;nbsp;Additionally, both flats fails to meet the built-in storage requirement. As well as, issues around stacking arrangements of the two flats. As such, the proposed development introduces sub-standard accommodation that will not facilitate an acceptable living standard for future occupiers, and represents a reduced standard of residential accommodation than the existing family sized dwelling. The proposed development is therefore contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC , 2021); - Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); - Policies CP3 and CC1 of the LDF Core Strategy (July 2010); - Policies BP6, BP8 and BP11 of the LDF Borough Wide Development Plan Policies DPD (March 2011); - Policies SP2, SP3 and DMD1 of the Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Submission version, December 2021); -DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
